#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t6/index.html:0
msgid "<0>11:00–11:30 · Talk · Talk 5: Verifying a card, sharing a link, and what you build today</0> (30 min). The trust ideas from Day 1 in practice. How an app reads a vaccination QR and checks it against the trust list, and how a shared health link is opened. Then a look at the four pieces the teams will build. <1>Leads:</1> Trust facilitator."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t1/index.html:0
msgid "<0>11:00–11:40 · Talk · Talk 1: Building with FHIR and the Open Health Stack</0> (40 min). A developer's tour of FHIR, then of the tools around it: the HAPI FHIR server, other open global goods, and where the OHS libraries and the OHS Player fit. <1>Leads:</1> Lead facilitator; <2>supports:</2> Co-facilitator."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t7/index.html:0
msgid "<0>11:30–12:30 · Team build · Team build, part 1</0> (60 min). Each team takes one app in the journey. Everything is pre-configured, so there is no Android Studio. You run the app, read how its configuration works, and change it. Test with the vaccination cards. <1>Leads:</1> Team facilitators; <2>supports:</2> One per team."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t2/index.html:0
msgid "<0>11:40–12:30 · Lab · Lab 1: Offline data capture</0> (50 min). The stack is already running on Heropa. Open a questionnaire in the form editor, change it, and watch the change appear in the OHS Player in your browser. Then add a validation rule or a skip rule. If time allows, see how the answers turn into FHIR resources. Optional: a QR code for the gallery app, to try the same forms on iOS or Android. <1>Leads:</1> Lab facilitator; <2>supports:</2> Co-facilitator."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t3/index.html:0
msgid "<0>13:30–13:50 · Talk · Talk 2: Trust between countries, SMART Trust and the GDHCN</0> (20 min). How a clinic in one country can trust a vaccination record from another. Covers the GDHCN network, digital vaccine certificates (DVC) and verifiable health links (VHL), and when to use a card and when to use a link. <1>Leads:</1> Trust facilitator."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t7/index.html:0
msgid "<0>13:30–14:25 · Team build · Team build, part 2</0> (55 min). Finish the change, test it with the cards, and get ready to show it. <1>Leads:</1> Team facilitators; <2>supports:</2> One per team."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t4/index.html:0
msgid "<0>13:50–14:00 · Talk · Talk 3: Workflows, sync and who sees what</0> (10 min). A short briefing before Lab 2. A plan definition says what should happen and when, such as the next vaccine due. Sync moves records between the device and the server. The gateway decides which records each user can reach. <1>Leads:</1> Co-facilitator; <2>supports:</2> Lab facilitator."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t4/index.html:0
msgid "<0>14:00–15:00 · Lab · Lab 2: Sync data and run a workflow</0> (60 min). In the Player, store records on the device and sync them to the server. Apply an immunization plan definition and see what comes due. Then sign in as two different users through the gateway and compare what each can see, for example 50 records against 10. <1>Leads:</1> Lab facilitator; <2>supports:</2> Co-facilitator."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t7/index.html:0
msgid "<0>14:25–15:00 · Showcase · Team presentations</0> (35 min). Each team shows what it built, about seven minutes each. Volunteers present. <1>Leads:</1> Lead facilitator (chair)."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t5/index.html:0
msgid "<0>15:30–15:40 · Talk · Talk 4: From records to charts</0> (10 min). How data gets out of the FHIR server and into tables you can chart. A look at FHIR Data Pipes, how one resource becomes a row, and what a dashboard reads. <1>Leads:</1> Data facilitator; <2>supports:</2> Lead facilitator."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t7/index.html:0
msgid "<0>15:30–16:15 · Team build · Putting the journey together</0> (45 min). Volunteers run the whole journey on the demo system, each using their own piece. This is the rehearsal for the finale. <1>Leads:</1> Team facilitators; <2>supports:</2> A volunteer from each team."
msgstr ""

#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/t5/index.html:0
msgid "<0>15:40–16:30 · Lab · Lab 3: Build your first dashboard</0> (50 min). A guided start in class, then a take-home task. Look at a dashboard built on the data from Lab 2. Add a small batch of new records, run the pipeline again and watch the chart update. Look at the audit events to see who accessed what. You then have about 24 hours to finish a dashboard of your own. <1>Leads:</1> Data facilitator."
msgstr ""

