#: en/smart-trust-demo/journeys/smart-trust-demo/workshops/technical-track/overview/index.html:0
msgid "The technical track of a general two-day workshop on verifiable immunization records across borders, taught from the journeys J1 to J4.1 of one cross-border family. It runs beside the [policy-maker track](../dpi-h-policy-track/) (M1 to M7): each technical module serves the policy module it is paired with, and both tracks meet in joint sessions each morning and at the close of each day. Two days, one cross-border immunization story. Day 1 covers the building blocks and gets everyone running on Heropa. Day 2 is teams building one part of the journey, then seeing it all work together. ## The two days A suggested timetable: a host adapts the times, and fills each country presentation with the host country or an invited country. ### Day 1 Concepts and the OHS stack. By the end of the day you have captured data, synced it, run a workflow and started a dashboard, all on Heropa. | Time | Session | |---|---| | 08:30–09:00 | Registration and Heropa login (Technical track: support crew) | | 09:00–10:30 | **Joint, both tracks:** FHIR around the world and the story we follow (Workshop hosts, with the policy track). P1.1 Welcome; P1.2 WHO remarks; P1.3 How the two days work; P1.4 Country panel; P1.5 Walkthrough of the five journeys | | 10:30–11:00 | Coffee, then move to the track rooms | | 11:00–12:30 | **Policy track, [M1](../dpi-h-policy-track/m1/):** From journey to capabilities | | 11:00–11:40 | **Technical track, [T1](t1/):** Talk 1: Building with FHIR and the Open Health Stack (talk) | | 11:40–12:30 | **Technical track, [T2](t2/):** Lab 1: Offline data capture (lab) | | 12:30–13:30 | Lunch | | 13:30–15:00 | **Policy track, [M2](../dpi-h-policy-track/m2/):** The reference architecture (DPI-H) and where you stand | | 13:30–13:50 | **Technical track, [T3](t3/):** Talk 2: Trust between countries, SMART Trust and the GDHCN (talk) | | 13:50–14:00 | **Technical track, [T4](t4/):** Talk 3: Workflows, sync and who sees what (talk) | | 14:00–15:00 | **Technical track, [T4](t4/):** Lab 2: Sync data and run a workflow (lab) | | 15:00–15:30 | Coffee | | 15:30–16:30 | **Policy track, [M3](../dpi-h-policy-track/m3/):** Standards, specifications and the core data set | | 15:30–15:40 | **Technical track, [T5](t5/):** Talk 4: From records to charts (talk) | | 15:40–16:30 | **Technical track, [T5](t5/):** Lab 3: Build your first dashboard (lab) | | 16:30–17:00 | **Joint, both tracks:** What we did today (Lead facilitator for the technical track). S1.1 Policy-maker track; S1.2 Technologist track; S1.3 Close of Day 1 | ### Day 2 Teams build one app in the journey, show it, and then everything runs together. | Time | Session | |---|---| | 08:30–09:00 | Arrival and Heropa login (Technical track: support crew) | | 09:00–10:30 | **Joint, both tracks:** Day 1 recap and today's plan (Workshop hosts). P2.1 Day 1 recap; P2.2 Host country digital health showcase; P2.3 Country vignettes; P2.4 Framing Day 2 | | 10:30–11:00 | Coffee, then back to the track rooms | | 11:00–11:30 | **Policy track, [M4](../dpi-h-policy-track/m4/):** Trust, credentials and wallets | | 11:00–11:30 | **Technical track, [T6](t6/):** Talk 5: Verifying a card, sharing a link, and what you build today (talk) | | 11:30–12:30 | **Policy track, [M5](../dpi-h-policy-track/m5/):** Governance, decision rights and the legal basis | | 11:30–12:30 | **Technical track, [T7](t7/):** Team build, part 1 (team build) | | 12:30–13:30 | Lunch | | 13:30–15:00 | **Policy track, [M6](../dpi-h-policy-track/m6/):** Doing it together | | 13:30–14:25 | **Technical track, [T7](t7/):** Team build, part 2 (team build) | | 14:25–15:00 | **Technical track, [T7](t7/):** Team presentations (showcase) | | 15:00–15:30 | Coffee, and set up the devices for the finale | | 15:30–16:15 | **Policy track, [M7](../dpi-h-policy-track/m7/):** First move and the investment required | | 15:30–16:15 | **Technical track, [T7](t7/):** Putting the journey together (team build) | | 16:15–16:30 | Move to the main room and brief the finale (Support crew) | | 16:30–17:00 | **Joint, both tracks:** The journey live, readouts and next steps (Lead facilitator with the workshop hosts). S2.1 Live demonstration; S2.2 Country first moves and the regional ask; S2.3 Handover | ## Before you run it - Agree the joint sessions on both days with the policy track, and who leads each closing slot. - Test the hosted classroom environment (Heropa) the week before. Day 2 apps need an emulator or the Wasm web build, since nobody installs Android Studio. - Lab 3: set up the dashboard tooling and the shared test data, with help on hand once the apps are seeded. - Assign a facilitator to each Day 2 team. - Record the full journey once as a fallback for the finale."
msgstr ""

